title: Emergency budget cuts
subtitle: Chancellor [+ chancellor +] proposes significant cuts to social spending.
new-page: true
view-if: (year == 1929 or year == 1930 or year == 1931 or year == 1932) and month >= 12 and chancellor == "Askew" and marcher_in_government == 0 and (disfavored > 15 or (year == 1929 and disfavored > 10)) and welfare >= -0 and war_loans > -2 and emergency_cuts_timer = 0
on-arrival: emergency_cuts_seen = 1; emergency_cuts_timer = 12; ddp_right += 1; gold_right += 1; lvp_right += 1; dufour_angry_bruning += 5
tags: event
max-visits: 4

= Emergency budget cuts

Due to the crisis of the Great Depression, government budgets have fallen and welfare spending has risen substantially. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] has used Article 48 of the constitution in order to pass an emergency bill cutting welfare spending.

[? if marcher_toleration : If we reject this, it would mean the end of the toleration agreement, and [+ chancellor +] would likely dissolve the Assembly and call new elections. Of course, the workers are opposed to this policy, although it might be necessary for economic and political stability. ?]

- @nothing_to_do: There is nothing we can do.
- @vote_no
- @vote_yes

@nothing_to_do
view-if: marcher_toleration == 0
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; disfavored += 1; disfavored_royalist += 3; disfavored_collectivist += 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; pro_republic -= 4; budget += 1; inflation -= 2; economic_growth -= 0.5;

The emergency policy passes under emergency rules, as the Assembly is currently dissolved. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> use this as a recruiting tool, and so do we.


@vote_no
title: Vote against this measure, ending the toleration agreement.
view-if: marcher_toleration
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 5; left_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 4; reformist_dissent += 8; left_dissent -= 5; gold_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; ddp_right += 1; gold_right += 2
call: set_next_election_time
go-to: new_prussia_election if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and ((center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"); center_right_coalition_prussia if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"

We have broken with the [+ chancellor +] government, and have voted against them in a vote of no confidence. Welfare has been saved, but at what cost?

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@new_prussia_election
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; collectivist_relation += 5; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; lvp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; landed_marcher -= 2; guild_marcher -= 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_royalist += 2; faithful_royalist += 2; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory vote in Heartland, forcing the dissolution of the state Assembly for new elections.

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland +].

A double dissolution has shaken the people's faith in democracy, with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> exploiting the instability to claim that democracy is unworkable, and that the Commonwealth needs a strong leader.

@center_right_coalition_prussia
on-arrival: in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 1; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0; heartland_leader = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; burgher_marcher -= 3; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.06; heartland_police_strength -= 8; 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory no confidence vote in Heartland, replacing our government with a center-right coalition composed of all parties to our right, except for the <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. While this is a setback, it is not the worst possible outcome, as new elections could have led to significant gains for extremist parties.

[? if unionist_leader != "Sedgewick": Adam Sedgewick?][? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": Edmund Askew?] of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is selected to be the Minister-President of Heartland.

@vote_yes
title: Vote in favor of this measure to continue the toleration agreement.
view-if: marcher_toleration
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; disfavored += 1; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; commons_marcher *= 0.92; disfavored_marcher *= 0.92; disfavored_royalist += 3; disfavored_collectivist += 3; commons_royalist += 3; commons_collectivist += 3; commons_marcher -= 3 if welfare < 0; disfavored_marcher -= 4 if welfare < 0; pro_republic -= 3; collectivist_relation -= 8; budget += 1; inflation -= 2; economic_growth -= 0.5

We try to convince the workers that this policy is necessary in order to maintain a stable parliamentary government, and to deal with the fiscal consequences of the depression. Still, this policy provides excellent recruiting fodder for <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
